@Oscar Pansy
English has been picking the pockets of any language within range since that little dust-up at Hastings in 1066. It started with Norman French back then and has continued up to, e.g., Viet Nam today. (Pho, anyone?)
Yesterday's Italian or Quechua will be today's (or, at the latest, tomorrow's) English. Prescriptivist though I may be, this is built into English's development.

